hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1395","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb told us, Muhammad bin Bishr told us, Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, so he mentioned the hadith in The story of the solar eclipse, and he said: When it was revealed, he, meaning the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and addressed the people, and they thanked God and praised Him, then he said: “The The sun and the moon are two signs of God that do not fail due to anyone’s death or his life, O nation of Muhammad. By God, there is no one more jealous than God who commits adultery. His servant or his female slave, O nation of Muhammad, by God or by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you knew what I know, you would have laughed little and wept much. Have I conveyed the message?”"
"1396","Abu Bakr said: In the report of Ibn Masoud, “the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, also gave a sermon before prayer.” During the eclipse, the imam should deliver the sermon before and after the prayer."
